From 03a2664a58b65a1611148c670a0181b90c4e745e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Enterprise OS <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:01:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(admin): scoped-key permissions and key status
 endpoint for directory sync

- Register users.create, users.update, users.api_keys.read,
  users.api_keys.create, api_keys.group.write and api_keys.status.write in
  the scoped admin key catalog (with zh/en labels).
- CreateForUser rejects administrator (403 ADMIN_USER_API_KEY_FORBIDDEN)
  and non-active users (403 USER_NOT_ACTIVE).
- Add PUT /api/v1/admin/api-keys/:id/status (active|disabled) via the
  owner-side APIKeyService.Update, which invalidates the auth cache.
  Expired/quota-exhausted keys cannot be re-enabled (409).
- Scoped keys cannot create, promote or modify administrators, cannot
  touch administrator-owned keys, and need users.balance.write to set a
  balance; user write responses follow read permissions.
- Explicit audit actions for the new routes; scoped-key audit records
  carry extra.route_action. Responses (plaintext keys) are never audited.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
